// Test: Middledot module paths in type position
// Spec: SIGIL_NATIVE_SYMBOLS_ROADMAP.md § path separator
// Priority: P1
//
// Purpose:
// Validates that `·` works as a path separator in a *type* position when the
// path begins with a lowercase module name, as in `std·fmt·Formatter`.
//
// The parser tells a type path (`HashMap·new`) from a method call on a variable
// (`tag·to_string`) by whether the first segment is uppercase. That heuristic
// belongs to expression position only: a type contains no variables, so every
// `·` in one is a path separator. Without the distinction a lowercase module
// path in a type is rejected -- which accounted for every one of the nihil
// tensor library's parse failures.
//
// Note the value is constructed through an import rather than through
// `geometry·Point { .. }`: a middledot module path in *expression* position is
// a separate, still-open gap, and this test is about the type position.
//
// Expected behavior:
// Should compile and print 42

☉ scroll geometry {
    ☉ Σ Point {
        ☉ x: !i32,
    }
}

invoke geometry·Point;

rite main() {
    ≔ p: geometry·Point = Point { x: 42 };
    println(p.x);
}
